# SPEC: 61_memory_management_DRAFT
# static-check: off
# Negative test (spec/61 §5.4): `.get`/`.at`/`.first`/`.last` on a container (list/map/cascade) or a
# Class-6 store (Kv/Store/TimeSeries/VecStore) yields a `ref<T>` BORROW — the container/store keeps
# ownership and never hands out a second owner. Binding that read to a `ptr<T>` (a UNIQUE OWNER) is a
# compile error: the borrow would be treated as owned and freed on drop/reassign (the historical
# test_model / db-reopen double-free). The spec-correct forms are `ref<T>` (borrow) or `get_copy`
# (an independent owned copy — which already exists).
#
# Expected: compilation fails (exit 1).  Before the §5.4 enforcement this compiled and could
# double-free the container's element box.

- model:
    name: Card
    fields:
      - [nam, string]

- def:
    name: main
    return: i32
    body:
      - decl: [deck, list<Card>]
      - decl: [one, Card]
      - set: [one.nam, "Ace"]
      - call: [deck.push, one]
      # ERROR: `.get` yields ref<Card>, not ptr<Card>. Bind ref<Card>, or use deck.get_copy(0).
      - decl: [bad, ptr<Card>, { call: [deck.get, 0] }]
      - print: ["UNEXPECTED_RUNTIME: ptr-bound borrow compiled ${bad.nam}"]
      - return: 0
